| `secrets.scanner.name` | string | `gitleaks` | one path part (no `/`, `\` or NUL, no leading `.` or surrounding whitespace): the scanner's program name | `scripts/scan_secrets.py` and `scripts/install_scanner.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `secrets.scanner.name` row | Names the release archive member `make secrets-install` installs and the program the record must name. `scripts/scan_secrets.py` adapts gitleaks only, so any other name is exit 14 before anything runs, in the scan and in `make secrets-install` alike (`scripts/scan_secrets.py` `other_adapter`): another scanner needs its own adapter, not only this value, because the flags the adapter passes are the scanner's own. Absent, the scan writes `[using default] secrets.scanner.name = "gitleaks"` to stderr. | choosing the release: `secrets.scanner.rev` | always |
